{title: 186 - I've Found a Friend}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #186 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 186}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]I've found a Friend; oh, such a Friend! He loved me ere [Db/Ab]I knew Him;
[Ab]He drew me [Gdim]with the [Fm]cords [Eb/Bb]of love, And [G7]thus He bound [Ab]me to Him.
[Ab]And 'round my heart still closely twine [Db/Ab]Those ties which nought can [Fm]sever,
[Ab]For I am [Bbm]His, and He is mine, Forever [Eb/Bb]and [Ab]forever.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]I've found a Friend; oh, such a [Db/Ab]Friend!
[Ab]He bled, He died to save [Db/Ab]me;
[Ab]And not [Gdim]alone [Eb]the [G7]gift of [Ab]life,
[Ab]But His [Gdim]own [Eb/Bb]self He [G7]gave [Ab]me.
[Ab]Nought that I have my [Db/Ab]own I [Fm]call,
[Ab]I hold it for [Db/Ab]the Giver;
[Ab]My heart, [Bbm]my strength, my [Eb/Bb]life my [Ab]all,
[Ab]Are His, [Bbm]and His forever.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]I've found a Friend; oh, such a [Db/Ab]Friend!
[Ab]All power to Him is given;
[Ab]To guard [Gdim]me [Fm]on [Eb]my [G7]upward [Ab]course,
[Ab]And bring [Gdim]me [Eb/Bb]safe to [G7]heaven.
[Ab]The eternal glories [Db/Ab]gleam afar,
[Ab]To nerve my faint [Db/Ab]endeavor;
[Ab]So now [Bbm]to watch, to [Eb/Bb]work, to [Ab]war,
[Ab]And then [Bbm]to rest forever.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Ab]I've found a Friend; oh, such a [Db/Ab]Friend!
[Ab]So kind, and true, and tender,
[Ab]So wise [Gdim]a [Fm]counselor [G7]and [Ab]guide,
[Ab]So mighty [Eb/Bb]a defender.
[Ab]From Him, who loveth [Db/Ab]me so [Fm]well,
[Ab]What power my soul [Db/Ab]can sever?
[Ab]Shall life [Bbm]or death, or [Eb/Bb]earth, or [Ab]hell?
[Ab]No; I [Bbm]am His forever.
{end_of_verse}
